{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he lifted his eyes and saw.</b> He saw with the physical sense of sight three men standing over him; and Scripture added the expression וירא a second time, to explain that he added seeing with the eye of the intellect and perceived them and recognized that they were angels. Therefore it says: וירץ לקראתם וישתחו ארצה. And these angels were Michael, Raphael, and Gabriel. Michael came to bring tidings to Sarah and to rescue Lot — these being two missions of kindness and mercy; Raphael to heal Abraham; Gabriel to overturn Sodom. And this is why it is written: ויבאו שני המלאכים סדומה בערב — and they are Michael and Gabriel: Michael to rescue Lot, Gabriel to overturn Sodom; and this is why it is written: ויהפך את הערים, and it does not say ויהפכו. And what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said — 'no single angel performs two missions' — they said only when the two are opposite to each other; for the angel appointed over mercy cannot be expected to perform judgment, which is its opposite, nor can the angel appointed over judgment come for mercy. But when the missions are both of judgment or both of mercy, he performs even several missions. Accordingly, you find that Michael performed two missions of kindness: the tidings of childbirth to one not fit to bear, and the rescue of Lot, who was not worthy of rescue. And if you should say that a third mission, healing, was also entrusted to him — since all of this falls under the category of kindness — no, that is not his domain, and he would thereby be encroaching on the boundary of Raphael. Therefore each one was entrusted with what lay within the power of his charge and appointment to perform, so as not to encroach on the boundary, for such is the law of the supernal beings, as it is written (Job 25:2): ״עושה שלום במרומיו״. And further, if you consider the parashah with insight, you will find that the Shekhinah was revealed to him here with its hosts, for these three angels are angels of the hosts, and they are from the four camps of the Shekhinah." "<b>And in Bereshit Rabbah:</b> In every place where you find Michael, there is the glory of the Shekhinah; and therefore when he saw them, he ran after them as one runs after the Shekhinah. And the reason why three were revealed and not all four, is all according to the need: the angel of kindness for two missions that were of kindness; the angel of mercy for the healing; the angel of judgment for the destruction of Sodom; and the fourth had already been revealed to him at the Covenant Between the Pieces. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:08.047038724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}